comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-20T03:19:36.131Z",maintainer-agent,"Duplicate check 2026-07-20: searched 'recovery bundle suggested_retry misleading flag' across all statuses — pm-6y58 (GH-500, built-in flag arity) and pm-9qcr (GH-507, extension contract arity) both FIXED and cover arity only; no existing item covers missing-flag PROVENANCE (mining flag tokens from error prose). Filed from the pm-ju83/6x7o/7ob5 graph-platform lane manual E2E."
  "2026-07-26T22:06:12.498Z","harness:claude-code","GitHub issue 757 is an instance of this class rather than a new defect. Same generator, same root cause: the recovery bundle derives flag suggestions from error-message prose instead of from the invoked command's declared flag contract. The new dimension it adds is cross-command leakage — --validate-close is a real pm flag, just not one pm update accepts — and a case where the correct recovery is a command redirect (use pm close) rather than any flag at all. Fixing this item must cover both: reject undeclared flags, and emit a command-level suggestion when no flag on the invoked command can resolve the failure. Sibling pm-ulqu stays separate: it is about rendering an enum flag's allowed values and about blocker ordering on a command that does accept the flag."
body: ""
